*  noend.sno -- a deck with no END card.
*  RUNAWAY: the compiler reads cards until it finds END, and there
*  is not one. On end-of-file the card-reading loop in the SIL source
*  branches to itself --
*
*      FORRUR STREAD  INBFSP,UNIT,FORRUR,COMP5
*
*  where the third operand is STREAD's EOF branch (S4D58 6.115) and it
*  is this instruction's own label -- so it reads for ever. A deck
*  without an END card hung the original too. Nothing stops this but
*  the instruction bound, which reports a *sil.Bound rather than a
*  fault, because the machine is working exactly as written.
*  Part of github.com/mdhender/sil. BSD 2-Clause; see LICENSE.
        OUTPUT = 'this never gets compiled'
